<title>UK: UK manufacturers, distributors stocks fall in Q3.</title>
<headline>UK manufacturers, distributors stocks fall in Q3.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics issued the following provisional data on manufacturers, wholesalers and retailers stocks in the third quarter of 1996 -</p>
<p>    STOCKS (in mln stg)     Q3		Q2	    Q3,95</p>
<p>    TOTAL			 -927	    -149	  1,255</p>
<p>    MANUFACTURING	     -176	    -215	  895</p>
<p>    WHOLESALING		 -462	     206	  156</p>
<p>    RETAILING		   -149		20	  218</p>
<p>MANUFACTURING BREAKDOWN</p>
<p>    MATERIALS AND FUEL	-212		56	  267</p>
<p>    WORK IN PROGRESS	    51	     128	  340</p>
<p>    FINISHED GOODS	     -15	    -399	  288</p>
<p>The ONS said the ratio of stocks to output fell to 90.6 at the end of September from 91.6 at the end of June. The ratio of retail stocks to sales fell to 105.8 at the end of September from 107.8 at the end of June.</p>
</text>
